B Counseling Internship Program and the Resiliency Initiative.       Three challenges:       Sport program support is challenging without enough staff to be present with each team each week. Presence provides opportunity for reduction of stigma and in turn produces more clients. Trinity and I have 8-9 teams with which to connect, and each program needs services even when they are out of season.        While the same number of sessions are being offered, the intensity of presenting problems is also increasing to include interpersonal violence, family trauma and bereavement, eating disorders, and problematic compulsive behaviors besides drug and alcohol use.       Innovation and productivity are challenged by campus wide budget constraints and the opportunity to set goals that need realistic funding parameters.                           Don Arterburn, 
